WEBVTT

00:00:00.387 --> 00:00:03.089
Build a tool once and the request stops

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.287
coming back to you: the job becomes a

00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:09.080
template other people fill in themselves,

00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:12.094
correctly, without you in the loop.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:16.501
Your work is plain HTML, CSS and

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:19.645
JavaScript - version-controlled, diffable,

00:00:19.702 --> 00:00:22.828
reviewable and running on an open engine,

00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:25.869
so it stays yours with nothing to unwind

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:27.044
later.

00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:30.401
Lolly is a platform-agnostic engine that

00:00:30.461 --> 00:00:32.896
runs the same render path across several

00:00:32.986 --> 00:00:36.142
shells - the web PWA, the desktop and

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.273
mobile apps, the CLI and the TUI - and

00:00:39.349 --> 00:00:42.882
tools are data rather than bundled code: a

00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:45.946
manifest, a template and optional hooks,

00:00:46.015 --> 00:00:49.570
so a new tool ships without an app update.

00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:53.128
Pick the lane below that matches what you

00:00:53.195 --> 00:00:55.118
are here to build.

00:00:55.911 --> 00:00:58.917
You are the multiplier in the relay: a

00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:01.773
creative authors the rules and you scale

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:05.364
them into a pipeline, a CLI batch or an

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:08.816
MCP endpoint, so The lifecycle of a

00:01:08.877 --> 00:01:11.461
campaign follows one asset through all

00:01:11.558 --> 00:01:13.544
three pairs of hands.

00:01:14.352 --> 00:01:15.806
New here?

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:19.412
The Quickstart gets a brand and your first

00:01:19.472 --> 00:01:22.395
render in place before you go deep.

00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:25.973
About states the licence boundary and the

00:01:26.034 --> 00:01:29.077
repositories each piece lives in, and

00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:31.849
Lolly for Operators is the door for

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:34.521
whoever will ask you about rollout and

00:01:34.582 --> 00:01:36.044
security.

00:01:37.169 --> 00:01:38.567
Designers

00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:42.475
Bring finished work in, set the rules once

00:01:42.533 --> 00:01:45.545
and keep the tools you already use.

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:49.275
What you decide here is what every tool in

00:01:49.315 --> 00:01:52.340
the gallery obeys, so a colour or a

00:01:52.405 --> 00:01:55.285
typeface is fixed in one place rather than

00:01:55.384 --> 00:01:57.719
argued about per asset.

00:01:58.503 --> 00:02:01.569
Import a design - bring a .

00:02:02.353 --> 00:02:03.324
fig, .

00:02:04.129 --> 00:02:05.322
penpot, .

00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:07.431
ai, .

00:02:08.215 --> 00:02:12.068
idml or SVG file in as an editable,

00:02:12.151 --> 00:02:14.672
re-renderable tool rather than a flat

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.869
picture.

00:02:16.641 --> 00:02:19.313
The Brand Studio - the on-device editor

00:02:19.457 --> 00:02:23.096
for logos, colours, type and the rest of

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.119
the design system «#/start».

00:02:26.885 --> 00:02:30.913
Design Tokens - the DTCG token model a

00:02:30.974 --> 00:02:34.235
brand is expressed in and how a tool reads

00:02:34.276 --> 00:02:36.170
it at render time.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.885
Authoring Assets - catalog assets, tiers,

00:02:39.943 --> 00:02:42.581
locales, palettes, themable icons and

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:43.744
fonts.

00:02:44.519 --> 00:02:47.252
The Dashboard - your design system shown

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:50.751
read-only, plus the capability map for the

00:02:50.813 --> 00:02:53.294
device in front of you.

00:02:54.419 --> 00:02:55.758
Developers

00:02:56.714 --> 00:02:59.934
One render path behind every surface: the

00:02:59.996 --> 00:03:03.120
GUI, the CLI and an agent all produce the

00:03:03.203 --> 00:03:06.020
same file from the same inputs.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.905
A tool is a manifest, a template and

00:03:09.971 --> 00:03:12.698
optional hooks, and every input is

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:16.395
expressible as a URL parameter, which is

00:03:16.477 --> 00:03:19.537
why a link and a command line are the same

00:03:19.611 --> 00:03:20.869
thing here.

00:03:21.632 --> 00:03:24.341
Architecture - why Lolly exists, the

00:03:24.432 --> 00:03:27.914
engine/shell/tool separation and the

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.545
commitments that hold it together.

00:03:31.306 --> 00:03:33.622
Authoring Tools - the full guide:

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.304
manifest, template, styles, hooks,

00:03:36.365 --> 00:03:38.694
composition and publishing.

00:03:39.466 --> 00:03:43.381
Host API - the HostV1 capability bridge

00:03:43.476 --> 00:03:46.271
every tool is written against, plus the

00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:49.469
note that hooks are not a sandbox.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:54.561
URL Mode - every input as a URL parameter:

00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:57.287
reserved params, compact encoding and

00:03:57.352 --> 00:03:58.744
packed links.

00:03:59.506 --> 00:04:02.270
Constraints - why output comes out right

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.074
by construction, with the tests that

00:04:05.131 --> 00:04:07.094
enforce each rule.

00:04:07.865 --> 00:04:11.573
Determinism - same inputs, same file: what

00:04:11.628 --> 00:04:14.969
is byte-reproducible and what is not.

00:04:15.738 --> 00:04:19.629
Reproducibility - the URL as the artifact,

00:04:19.688 --> 00:04:22.719
and how far a bare link can carry.

00:04:23.484 --> 00:04:25.983
CLI - headless rendering over the same

00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:30.114
path as the GUI, driven by --foo=bar argv

00:04:30.176 --> 00:04:31.319
pairs.

00:04:32.115 --> 00:04:34.469
Signing from the terminal - give CLI

00:04:34.557 --> 00:04:38.326
output a real signing identity instead of

00:04:38.405 --> 00:04:40.969
an anonymous on-device key.

00:04:41.737 --> 00:04:44.785
TUI - the interactive terminal shell, for

00:04:44.847 --> 00:04:48.269
when a pipeline needs a human in it.

00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:52.830
MCP Server - the native endpoint an AI

00:04:52.898 --> 00:04:56.619
agent uses to discover and run tools.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.653
AI Agents - driving Lolly from a model,

00:05:00.713 --> 00:05:03.994
where a URL is the API.

00:05:04.741 --> 00:05:08.270
Browser Extension - capture a live URL as

00:05:08.355 --> 00:05:12.320
a reusable asset for a tool to compose.

00:05:13.077 --> 00:05:16.343
Content Credentials Identity - CA-issued

00:05:16.414 --> 00:05:19.848
signing for on-device C2PA, with the

00:05:19.927 --> 00:05:22.805
engine contracts behind what an export

00:05:22.866 --> 00:05:24.069
carries.

00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:26.695
Infrastructure

00:05:27.629 --> 00:05:30.906
For standalone use, deploy static files or

00:05:30.971 --> 00:05:34.065
a prepared air-gapped app; local rendering

00:05:34.127 --> 00:05:35.944
needs no server.

00:05:36.729 --> 00:05:39.874
For organisation identity, policy and

00:05:39.969 --> 00:05:42.764
shared work, add lolly-work, the Lolly

00:05:42.826 --> 00:05:45.869
project's separately deployed service.

00:05:46.619 --> 00:05:49.865
It also offers persistent render jobs and

00:05:49.926 --> 00:05:52.344
batches for automation.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.696
Deployment - the web app, packaged apps,

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.115
optional integrations and lolly-work:

00:05:58.172 --> 00:06:00.220
where each piece runs.

00:06:00.983 --> 00:06:04.140
Organisation automation - use lolly-work's

00:06:04.224 --> 00:06:08.615
lw client and authenticated API for queued

00:06:08.675 --> 00:06:12.145
renders, batches and governed delivery.

00:06:12.898 --> 00:06:16.048
Configuration - profiles, brand packs,

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.682
capability gating, feature flags and

00:06:18.746 --> 00:06:20.770
catalog validation.

00:06:21.531 --> 00:06:24.265
Build Guide - build every target: CLI,

00:06:24.339 --> 00:06:28.369
TUI, desktop, mobile and the web PWA.

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:32.341
Building for iOS - the extra gates Apple

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:36.139
adds, and what a device build needs on top

00:06:36.175 --> 00:06:38.144
of the desktop one.

00:06:38.891 --> 00:06:41.228
Contributing Setup - a development

00:06:41.277 --> 00:06:44.433
checkout sized to what you are here to do,

00:06:44.516 --> 00:06:46.970
from a slim clone upward.

00:06:47.738 --> 00:06:50.795
Data Transfer - the lolly-backup bundle:

00:06:50.872 --> 00:06:53.462
envelope, integrity and the cross-shell

00:06:53.523 --> 00:06:54.994
guarantees.

00:06:55.775 --> 00:06:58.271
Threat Model & Trust Boundaries - what

00:06:58.339 --> 00:07:01.378
Lolly defends against, what it does not

00:07:01.438 --> 00:07:04.073
and where each boundary falls, before a

00:07:04.134 --> 00:07:05.694
review asks.
